BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the conceptual framework of engineering drawing as the universal language of engineers, detailing the role of national \(BIS\) and international \(ISO\) standards.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Foundation of Engineering Drawing:) Tj
T*
(   Engineering drawing is the formal, rigorous graphic language employed by engineers, architects,) Tj
T*
(   and technical professionals worldwide to convey geometric configurations, physical dimensions,) Tj
T*
(   material specifications, and manufacturing tolerances without ambiguity.) Tj
T*
(   Unlike artistic expressions, technical drawings adhere to standardized geometric rules so that) Tj
T*
(   any engineer across the globe can interpret and fabricate the intended component identically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Standardization Framework:) Tj
T*
(   - International Organization for Standardization \(ISO\): Standardizes technical drawings) Tj
T*
(   globally through Technical Committee ISO/TC 10 \(e.g., ISO 128 for general principles of) Tj
T*
(   presentation, ISO 129 for dimensioning, ISO 5456 for projection methods, ISO 7200 for title) Tj
T*
(   blocks\).) Tj
T*
(   - Bureau of Indian Standards \(BIS\): Formulates Indian national standards aligned with ISO,) Tj
T*
(   specifically compiled in the code of practice SP 46:2003 \('Engineering Drawing Practice for) Tj
T*
(   Schools and Colleges'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Key Core Objectives:) Tj
T*
(   - Unambiguous communication between design and manufacturing teams.) Tj
T*
(   - Comprehensive geometric definition \(shape, size, surface quality, fit\).) Tj
T*
(   - Traceability, design revision management, and legal contract documentation in commercial) Tj
T*
(   production.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
