(   [Problem Statement]: Classify and describe the standard drawing instruments used in manual drafting, including their proper maintenance and handling procedures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Essential Drawing Instruments:) Tj
T*
(   - Drawing Board: Made of seasoned knot-free softwood \(pine or fir\) with a straight ebony edge) Tj
T*
(   on the left to guide the T-square. Standard sizes: D0 \(1500x1000 mm\), D1 \(1000x700 mm\), D2) Tj
T*
(   \(700x500 mm\), D3 \(500x350 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - T-Square: Comprises a wooden or plastic stock and blade joined rigidly at 90 degrees. Used) Tj
T*
(   for drawing horizontal parallel lines and supporting set-squares.) Tj
T*
(   - Mini-Drafter: A precision pantograph mechanism clamped to the top edge of the board. Features) Tj
T*
(   two graduated orthogonal blades that maintain parallel alignment across the entire sheet,) Tj
T*
(   replacing T-squares, set-squares, and protractors.) Tj
T*
(   - Set-Squares: Acrylic triangular rulers in pairs \(45?-45? and 30?-60?\). Used individually or) Tj
T*
(   in combination to construct angles in 15? increments.) Tj
T*
(   - Engineering Compasses: Large bow compass for circles up to 150 mm radius \(with lengthening) Tj
T*
(   bar for larger radii\) and spring bow compass for high-precision small circles \(< 25 mm radius\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dividers: Plain dividers and spring bow dividers used for stepping off equal distances and) Tj
T*
(   transferring dimensions from scale rulers.) Tj
T*
(   - French Curves & Flexible Splines: Templates with varying curvature for drawing smooth) Tj
T*
(   mathematical curves passing through discrete plotted points.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Maintenance and Care:) Tj
T*
(   - Clean acrylic blades regularly with mild soapy water; never scrape edges with metal razor) Tj
T*
(   blades.) Tj
T*
ET

