(   [Problem Statement]: Categorize and describe the standard line types used in engineering drawing as per BIS SP 46:2003 \(ISO 128\), including their thicknesses, applications, and pencil selection.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Standard Line Classification Table \(BIS SP 46 / ISO 128\):) Tj
T*
(   - Type A: Continuous Thick Line \(~0.50 mm, Grade H/HB\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Visible outlines, visible edges, crests of external screw threads.) Tj
T*
(   - Type B: Continuous Thin Line \(~0.25 mm, Grade 2H/3H\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Dimension lines, extension lines, leader lines, hatching lines, construction) Tj
T*
(   lines, projection lines, revolved section outlines.) Tj
T*
(   - Type C: Continuous Thin Freehand Line \(~0.25 mm, Grade 2H\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Limits of partial or interrupted views and sections when boundary is not an axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Type D: Continuous Thin Line with Zigzags \(~0.25 mm, Grade 2H\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Long break lines across shafts and structural members.) Tj
T*
(   - Type E / F: Dashed Thin Line \(~0.25 mm, Grade 2H\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Hidden outlines and hidden edges \(dash length 3 mm, spacing 1 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Type G: Chain Thin Line \(Long dash-dot, ~0.25 mm, Grade 2H/3H\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Center lines, axes of symmetry, pitch circle paths. \(Dash 10-12 mm, space 1 mm,) Tj
T*
(   dot 1 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Type H: Chain Thin Line with Thick Ends and Direction Change \(~0.25 mm thin with ~0.50 mm) Tj
T*
(   ends\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Cutting plane traces indicating position and viewing direction of cross-sections.) Tj
T*
(   - Type J: Chain Thick Line \(~0.50 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Indication of surfaces to receive secondary specialized surface treatment.) Tj
T*
(   - Type K: Chain Thin Double-Dash Line \(~0.25 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   Application: Outlines of adjacent parts, extreme alternate positions of movable mechanical) Tj
T*
(   linkages, centroidal axes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rules of Line Precedence:) Tj
T*
(   When two lines of different types occupy the exact same coordinate path:) Tj
T*
(   1st: Visible outlines \(Type A\) take highest priority.) Tj
T*
(   2nd: Hidden outlines \(Type E/F\).) Tj
T*
(   3rd: Cutting plane lines \(Type H\).) Tj
T*
(   4th: Center lines and axes of symmetry \(Type G\).) Tj
T*
(   5th: Construction and dimension extension lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
