(   [Problem Statement]: Design and construct a diagonal scale of RF = 1:5000 to show kilometers, hectometers, and decameters, suitable for reading up to 1 km. Provide all calculations and describe the procedure to indicate 6 hectometers and 7 decameters.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   - Given: RF = 1 / 5,000.) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum Length to measure \(ML\) = 1 km = 1,000 meters = 100,000 cm.) Tj
T*
(   - Length of Scale \(LOS\) = RF x ML = \(1 / 5,000\) x 100,000 cm = 20.0 cm \(200 mm\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Scale Division Structure:) Tj
T*
(   - 1 km = 10 Hectometers \(hm\); 1 hm = 10 Decameters \(dam\).) Tj
T*
(   - Divide total length of 200 mm into 10 equal main divisions.) Tj
T*
(   Each main division = 20 mm, representing 1 hectometer \(0.1 km = 1 hm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total length represents 10 hm = 1 km.) Tj
T*
(   - Place zero '0' at the 1st division mark from left. Mark 0 to 9 hm to the right.) Tj
T*
(   - The leftmost 1-hm division is divided into 10 parts, each = 1 decameter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Diagonal Principle Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   - Construct vertical scale rectangle of height 50 mm \(divided into 10 equal horizontal parallel) Tj
T*
(   lines spaced 5 mm apart\).) Tj
T*
(   - Join sub-divisions diagonally: Connect 0 of bottom line to 1 of top line; 1 of bottom to 2 of) Tj
T*
(   top; ... 9 of bottom to 10 of top.) Tj
T*
(   - By principle of similar right triangles, the horizontal offset increases by 0.1 of a unit at) Tj
T*
(   each successive horizontal line.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Measuring 6 Hectometers and 7 Decameters \(0.67 km\):) Tj
T*
(   - Locate main division mark 6 hm to the right of 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Move to the 7th horizontal line above the baseline \(representing 7 decameters\).) Tj
T*
(   - Follow the 7th diagonal line to the left of 0 up to its intersection with horizontal line 7.) Tj
T*
(   - Distance between these points is exactly 6 hm + 7 dam = 67 dam = 670 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Draw extension lines, dimension line, and label '670 m \(6 hm 7 dam\)'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 11:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
