(   - Let ABC be a right-angled triangle where base BC has a unit length 's' \(e.g., 1 mm or 1) Tj
T*
(   sub-unit\) and vertical altitude AB has arbitrary drafting height 'h' \(e.g., 50 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Divide altitude AB into 'n' equal parts \(typically n = 10\) by horizontal lines parallel to) Tj
T*
(   base BC, labeled 1, 2, 3, ... n from top A down to base B.) Tj
T*
(   - Let 1-1', 2-2', ... k-k' represent the horizontal lines at heights h1, h2, ... hk from apex) Tj
T*
(   A.) Tj
T*
(   - By properties of similar triangles \(Triangle A-k-k' is similar to Triangle A-B-C\):) Tj
T*
(   \(k-k'\) / BC = \(A-k\) / AB = k / n.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: Length of horizontal segment \(k-k'\) = \(k / n\) * BC = \(k / n\) * s.) Tj
T*
(   - For n = 10:) Tj
T*
(   * At 1st division from apex: length = 1/10 * s = 0.1 s.) Tj
T*
(   * At 2nd division: length = 2/10 * s = 0.2 s.) Tj
T*
(   * At 7th division: length = 7/10 * s = 0.7 s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Resolution Advantage:) Tj
T*
(   This geometric magnification converts a direct linear division of 0.1 mm \(which is impossible) Tj
T*
(   to draw manually with a pencil\) into a vertical step of 5 mm, achieving 10x greater drafting) Tj
T*
(   precision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
