/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Compare plain scales, diagonal scales, and vernier scales, summarizing their measurement capabilities, structural layout, and specific engineering applications.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Plain Scales:) Tj
T*
(   - Capability: Measures two consecutive dimensional units \(e.g. meters and decimeters, or feet) Tj
T*
(   and inches\) or a single unit down to its first decimal place.) Tj
T*
(   - Structure: A single linear horizontal bar divided into primary divisions, with only the) Tj
T*
(   leftmost division subdivided into secondary units.) Tj
T*
(   - Application: General architectural drawings, basic site plans, standard structural) Tj
T*
(   elevations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Diagonal Scales:) Tj
T*
(   - Capability: Measures three consecutive units \(e.g. meters, decimeters, centimeters; or yards,) Tj
T*
(   feet, inches\) or two decimal places.) Tj
T*
(   - Structure: A 2D grid combining vertical equidistant divisions with diagonal sloping lines) Tj
T*
(   across the leftmost block.) Tj
T*
(   - Application: Cadastral land surveys, railway maps, precision machine templates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Vernier Scales:) Tj
T*
(   - Capability: Achieves ultra-high resolution via an auxiliary sliding or graduated plate where) Tj
T*
(   'n' vernier divisions equal \(n - 1\) or \(n + 1\) main scale divisions.) Tj
T*
(   - Structure: Main scale accompanied by a sliding vernier index; eliminates the need for tall) Tj
T*
(   vertical diagonal grids.) Tj
T*
(   - Application: Precision workshop metrology \(Vernier calipers, micrometers, theodolites\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
