(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the setup procedure for an AutoCAD drawing session for an A3 engineering sheet in millimeters, detailing all commands executed from scratch.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Complete Step-by-Step AutoCAD Setup Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   1. Initialize New Drawing:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: NEW -> Select template 'acadiso.dwt' \(standard ISO metric template\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Configure Drawing Units \(UNITS command\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: UNITS [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - Set Linear Type: Decimal | Precision: 0.00) Tj
T*
(   - Set Insertion Scale Units: Millimeters) Tj
T*
(   - Set Angular Format: Decimal Degrees | Precision: 0) Tj
T*
(   - Click OK.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Establish Drawing Limits \(LIMITS command\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LIMITS [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - Specify lower-left corner: 0,0 [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - Specify upper-right corner: 420,297 [Enter] \(Standard ISO A3 sheet\).) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LIMITS -> Enter option: ON [Enter] \(Enforces boundary\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Configure Drafting Grid and Snap:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: DSETTINGS [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - Under 'Snap and Grid' tab: Set Grid X & Y spacing = 10 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Uncheck 'Display grid beyond Limits'. Set Snap spacing = 5 mm. Click OK.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Reset Viewport Zoom \(ZOOM ALL\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: ZOOM [Enter] -> Option: A [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Viewport fits the 420x297 mm workspace perfectly to screen.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   6. Setup Standard Layers \(LAYER command\):) Tj
T*
(   - Layer '0_Border': Color White/Black, Continuous, Lineweight 0.50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 'Visible_Outlines': Color Blue, Continuous, Lineweight 0.50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 'Hidden_Lines': Color Cyan, Linetype HIDDEN, Lineweight 0.25 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 'Center_Lines': Color Red, Linetype CENTER, Lineweight 0.25 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 'Dimensions': Color Green, Continuous, Lineweight 0.25 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
