(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the causes and remedies of common line appearance errors in AutoCAD, such as hidden and center lines appearing solid, detailing LTSCALE, PSLTSCALE, and REGEN.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Nature of the Problem:) Tj
T*
(   In AutoCAD, non-continuous linetypes \(e.g., HIDDEN, CENTER, PHANTOM\) often display as solid) Tj
T*
(   continuous lines on screen or in layout viewports.) Tj
T*
(   This occurs because the default dash and gap pattern lengths are either excessively large) Tj
T*
(   compared to the drawn feature or infinitely small relative to screen zoom.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Global Linetype Scaling \(LTSCALE\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Sets the global scaling factor applied to all non-continuous linetypes across the) Tj
T*
(   entire drawing database.) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LTSCALE [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - If dashed lines appear solid on a 420x297 mm sheet, the default scale factor \(often 1.0\) is) Tj
T*
(   too large.) Tj
T*
(   - Solution: Enter a smaller factor such as 0.5 or 0.25 \(or larger, e.g. 10 or 20, if working in) Tj
T*
(   huge architectural meter units\).) Tj
T*
(   - Execute REGEN [Enter] to force AutoCAD to recalculate line display vectors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Paper Space Linetype Scaling \(PSLTSCALE\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Controls whether linetypes in layout viewports are scaled based on viewport zoom) Tj
T*
(   factor or paper space units.) Tj
T*
(   - PSLTSCALE = 1 \(Default & Recommended\): Dash and gap lengths display identically on paper) Tj
T*
(   regardless of individual viewport zoom scales.) Tj
T*
(   - PSLTSCALE = 0: Linetype dash lengths scale proportionally to viewport zoom magnification.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Current Entity Linetype Scale \(CELTSCALE\):) Tj
T*
(   - Sets individual scale overrides for newly created objects. Should strictly remain set to 1.0) Tj
T*
(   to avoid confusing per-object scale inconsistencies.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
