/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A map is drawn to a scale such that 1 cm represents 250 meters. Construct a comparative scale to read distances in miles and furlongs up to 4 miles. Provide complete mathematical conversions and drafting steps.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Calculations and RF:) Tj
T*
(   - Given Primary Scale: 1 cm = 250 meters = 25,000 cm.) Tj
T*
(   - Representative Fraction \(RF\) = 1 / 25,000.) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum Length to measure on comparative scale = 4 miles.) Tj
T*
(   - Imperial to Metric Conversion:) Tj
T*
(   * 1 mile = 1.60934 km = 160,934 cm.) Tj
T*
(   * 4 miles = 4 x 160,934 cm = 643,736 cm.) Tj
T*
(   - Length of Comparative Scale \(LOS\):) Tj
T*
(   LOS = RF x ML = \(1 / 25,000\) x 643,736 cm = 25.75 cm \(257.5 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since 25.75 cm is too long for an A4/A3 sheet, reduce maximum measuring capacity to 3 miles:) Tj
T*
(   * For ML = 3 miles = 3 x 160,934 cm = 482,802 cm:) Tj
T*
(   * LOS = \(1 / 25,000\) x 482,802 cm = 19.31 cm = 193.1 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Scale Division Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - 1 mile = 8 furlongs.) Tj
T*
(   - Draw horizontal scale bar of length 193.1 mm and divide into 3 equal primary parts.) Tj
T*
(   Each primary part represents 1 mile \(length = 193.1 / 3 = 64.37 mm per mile\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mark zero '0' at the 1st division. Number 1, 2 miles to the right.) Tj
T*
(   - Subdivide the leftmost 1-mile division \(64.37 mm\) into 8 equal parts.) Tj
T*
(   Each subdivision represents 1 furlong \(64.37 mm / 8 = 8.05 mm per furlong\).) Tj
T*
(   - Number furlongs from 0 towards the left: 0, 2, 4, 6, 8 furlongs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Verification and Marking:) Tj
T*
(   - To show a distance of 2 miles and 5 furlongs:) Tj
T*
(   * Measure 2 miles to the right of zero.) Tj
T*
(   * Measure 5 furlongs to the left of zero.) Tj
T*
(   * Distance between marks equals 2 miles 5 furlongs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
