ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the drafting methodology for dividing a circle into 12 equal parts using only standard set-squares and a compass, detailing its application in engineering projections.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Significance:) Tj
T*
(   Dividing a circle into 12 equal sectors \(30? intervals\) is one of the most critical) Tj
T*
(   construction techniques in engineering drawing, essential for orthographic projections of) Tj
T*
(   cylinders, cones, screws, and surface developments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Construction Using Compass and T-Square:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw a circle of given radius R with center O.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Draw horizontal centerline AB \(using T-square\) and vertical centerline CD \(using) Tj
T*
(   set-square perpendicular to T-square\). Points A, B, C, D divide the circle into 4 quadrants) Tj
T*
(   \(0?, 90?, 180?, 270?\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: With compass set strictly to the circle radius R:) Tj
T*
(   * Strike arcs from point A cutting circle at points 1 and 11.) Tj
T*
(   * Strike arcs from point B cutting circle at points 5 and 7.) Tj
T*
(   * Strike arcs from point C cutting circle at points 2 and 4.) Tj
T*
(   * Strike arcs from point D cutting circle at points 8 and 10.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: The circle is now divided into 12 perfectly equal parts spaced at 30-degree intervals) Tj
T*
(   \(360? / 12 = 30?\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Alternative Method Using 30?-60? Set-Square:) Tj
T*
(   - Place 30?-60? set-square on the T-square edge.) Tj
T*
(   - Draw diameter lines through center O at 30?, 60?, 120?, and 150? to the horizontal.) Tj
T*
(   - Together with horizontal \(0?-180?\) and vertical \(90?-270?\) diameters, the circle is) Tj
T*
(   partitioned into 12 equal sectors in under 30 seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
